{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Let me sip, I pray, etc.</b> Now, he diminished from what he had stipulated to ask, for he had said he would say to her: ״Tilt your jar, I pray, and I will drink,״ yet now he said <b>הַגְמִיאִינִי</b> — meaning the expression of sipping — and he also said <b>מְעַט</b> (״a little״), and he also did not say that she should tilt her jar herself to give him to drink as he had stipulated. His reason is according to the words of the Sages, may their memory be for blessing (Genesis Rabbah 60:9), that he saw the waters rose up toward her, and this sign was a clear one that is not found among the daughters of the Canaanite but only in a blessed and holy seed such as Abraham's; also, his mazal showed him that she is the one. Therefore he was afraid concerning the conditions he had stipulated — lest she not fulfill them and he thereby lose what he sought on account of his conditions. Therefore he minimized in every possible way in his conditions, so that it would be easy in her eyes to fulfill them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:03.269022012Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}